#
# Clean conformance fixture for math:IncompleteConfidenceIntervalShape (Rule I4) and
# math:IntervalKindConflationShape (Rule I3): a math:ConfidenceInterval carrying its two
# bounds through math:hasIntervalBound (a lower AND an upper endpoint, satisfying
# sh:minCount 2) and its coverage through math:confidenceLevel — a FRAMED
# math:ProbabilityValue, exact 95/100 in [0, 1] per the exact-rational discipline (AC#6),
# so the level satisfies math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape / math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape /
# math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape / math:RationalValueShape. It is NOT typed
# math:CredibleInterval, so math:IntervalKindConflationShape's sh:not stays satisfied.
# It MUST raise NO failure class.
# Positive counterpart of counter-examples/confidence-interval-incomplete.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConfidenceIntervalComplete).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:meanCI a math:ConfidenceInterval ;
    math:hasIntervalBound ex:ciLower , ex:ciUpper ;
    math:confidenceLevel ex:ciLevel .

ex:ciLower a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:ciUpper a math:MathematicalObject .

# The coverage: a FRAMED probability value, exact 95/100 = 0.95 in [0, 1].
ex:ciLevel a math:ProbabilityValue , math:RationalValue ;
    math:numerator 95 ;        # 95/100 = 0.95, within [0, 1]
    math:denominator 100 ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:samplingFrame .

ex:samplingFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/ciLevel> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
